BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: Ken Dewitt
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T143000
UID:260606d18siiiDVEq1IlTej3hvIA
DESCRIPTION:Chillax with Sir Uke: Ken Dewitt Live\n\nJoin us for No Cell S
 undays with Ken Dewitt\, affectionately known as "Sir Uke"—a North Bay u
 kulele player whose warm\, charming style pairs perfectly with a lazy Sund
 ay afternoon.\n\nSir Uke's soothing covers of beloved songs\, played on th
 e enchanting ukulele\, create a laid-back and inviting atmosphere that mel
 ts away the week's stress. With melodies that drift effortlessly through t
 he air\, his music is the perfect soundtrack for unwinding\, sipping wine\
 , and simply enjoying the moment.\n\nWhether you're sprawled on a blanket 
 under the sun or settled in with a glass of your favorite vintage\, Sir Uk
 e delivers exactly what you need: good vibes\, great music\, and zero stre
 ss.\n\nWhat's No Cell Sundays?\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your device
 s\, reconnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people around you. Ch
 eck your phone with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting. Br
 ing a blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was meant 
 to be spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-ken-dewitt
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NAPA PRIDE: Drag Brunch at The Charles Napa\, Supporting LGBTQ Con
 nection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T130000
UID:260604XhBmu-Rw4UufzPIYyN-x9w
DESCRIPTION:***Napa Pride Drag Brunch at The Charles***\n\nJoin us in pers
 on for an unforgettable drag brunch immediately preceding the official kic
 k-off of **Napa Pride**. Hosted at **The Charles Napa Valley** at 1301 
 Jefferson Street in downtown Napa\, this lively courtyard event will featu
 re fabulous performances by the iconic **Countess Katya Smirnoff-Skyy**
  and **Ava LaShay**\, a delicious brunch menu\, the option to add endles
 s mimosas\, and support for a vital charitable cause.\n\nA portion of the 
 proceeds will benefit **LGBTQ Connection**\, a program of local nonprofit
  **On The Move Bay Area**. Come hungry\, ready to cheer\, and ready to ha
 ve a blast with friends old and new.\n\nKatya Smirnoff-Skyy and Ava LaShay
  are two of the Bay Area's most celebrated drag performers\, singers\, and
  comedians. Guests will enjoy a pre-selected brunch entrée\, tableside mi
 mosa service\, photo opportunities with Katya\, remarks from LGBTQ Connect
 ion\, and a small silent auction supporting local queer community work.\n\
 nThe brunch takes place immediately before Napa Pride’s official kick-of
 f **Tea Dance** at Andaz Mercantile Terrace in downtown Napa. After brun
 ch\, guests are encouraged to continue the celebration at the Tea Dance\, 
 just an 8-minute walk from The Charles.\n\nNote: If you are driving to dow
 ntown Napa and plan to attend the Tea Dance after our brunch\, we encourag
 e you to park at The Andaz or in public parking facilities in downtown Nap
 a. Parking at The Charles is limited. It's an easy 8-min walk from the And
 az to the hotel.\n\n***Pride Brunch Menu***\n\nAfter selecting your ticket
 (s)\, you will be presented with a menu of food options to choose from. Pl
 ease make a selection by June 6\; your registration can be edited until th
 en.\n\nOptions include the following\, with a choice of two sides (regular
  or gluten-free toast\, sausage links\, assorted fruits and berries\, slic
 ed avocado\, plus various accoutrements).\n\n\\- Golden waffles with fresh
  fruit + sides\n\n\\- Savory egg and vegetable casserole + sides\n\n\\- He
 arty egg\, sausage\, and cheese casserole + sides\n\n\\- Greek yogurt with
  layered fruit and granola + sides\n\n\\- Avocado toast (vegan) + sides\n\
 n***About The Charles Napa Valley***\n\nThe Charles Napa Valley is an art
 fully designed\, gay-owned boutique hotel in downtown Napa\, built on incl
 usive hospitality\, classical design\, and warm\, personal service. For th
 is event\, The Charles will host guests in its beautiful courtyard\, shade
 d by mature orange and Japanese maple trees\, with comfortable outdoor fur
 niture and multiple fountains.\n\n***Guest Notes***\n\nGuests must be 21+ 
 to consume alcohol. Please select your brunch menu choice when purchasing 
 your ticket. Seating is limited\, and the courtyard comfortably seats abou
 t 45 guests. Bring cash to tip the performers and participate in nonprofit
  fundraising opportunities through the art and silent auctions.\n\n***Agen
 da***\n\n**11:00 AM**\n\nGuest Arrival & Photos with Katya Smirnoff-Skyy a
 nd Ava LaShay\n\n**11:30 AM - 01:00 PM**\n\nAlternating performances fea
 t. live singing and comedy\, with periodic intermissions.\n\n**01:00 PM**\
 n\nHead to the official Napa Pride kick-off at The Andaz Hotel
LOCATION:The Charles Napa Valley
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1989622952811/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sister Act
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T163000
UID:2606045k1lVc7TyEqRcj7x90HV2A
DESCRIPTION:Sister Act is the high-energy musical comedy based on the belo
 ved 1992 film. Featuring an electrifying Alan Menken score infused with di
 sco and gospel beats\, this feel-good show is a celebration of music\, sis
 terhood\, and second chances. When disco diva Deloris Van Cartier witnesse
 s a crime\, she’s forced into hiding—in a convent! Disguised as a nun\
 , she transforms the struggling choir with her powerhouse voice\, helping 
 them find their sound while discovering her own. Nominated for five Tony A
 wards\, Sister Act is a joyful\, soul-stirring spectacle that proves music
 —and a little mischief—can work miracles
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/907119495682865/907119502349531/?activ
 e_tab=about
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
