BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free pipe-organ concert in Healdsburg June 7
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T180000
UID:260603j3Doi0VFoEO0Io5kQwGVng
DESCRIPTION:Members of the Redwood Empire Chapter of the American Guild of
  Organists will play selections on the Bigelow pipe organ installed inside
  St. Paul's Episcopal Church at 5 p.m. Sunday\, June 7. The public is welc
 ome to attend this free concert\, which is the last in the 2025-26 season.
  Concerts are on hiatus in July and August but will return Sept. 20 with a
  performance by Alexander Valley resident David Hatt. Donations to the chu
 rch's building maintenance fund will be gladly accepted. Those who cannot 
 attend the live performance may watch it later online at www.stpauls-heald
 sburg.org/sunday\\_organ\\_series. The concerts are a gift of music to the
  public\, from the church\, to provide an opportunity to hear classical mu
 sic at no charge. The church is located at the corner of East and Matheson
  Streets\, one block east of Healdsburg's downtown Plaza.
LOCATION:St. Paul's Episcopal Church
URL:http://www.stpauls-healdsburg.org/sunday_organ_series
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
