BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Goodspeed Trail Wildflower & Nature Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T120000
UID:260526Dz3uBIOgL0e5p-Z7cNGzug
DESCRIPTION:We will be looking for late spring and early summer 
 blooms\, contrasting plant communities associated with lush canyon
  riparian areas and dry serpentine chaparral hillsides\, and seei
 ng examples of how some flowering plants communicate with pollina
 tors. This is a 3-3.5 mile out-and-back hike. There will be a l
 ow level stream crossing and some moderate hillside climbing\, th
 ough we will turn around well before the Nattkemper bench. \n\nM
 eet at the Goodspeed parking lot. Tickets are $10 for general a
 udiences\, $5 for students\, youth \\(12-17 year olds\; must be 
 accompanied by a parent or legal guardian\\)\, Sugarloaf  members
 \, Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers\, and free for children 7-11. Not
  recommended for children younger than 7. Tickets day-of on site
  are $15 and might not be available. Wear comfortable clothing\,
  appropriate footwear for rocky/slippery trails\, and sun protecti
 on. Bring at least a quart of water\, hiking poles\, and if yo
 u desire\, a snack. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/goodspeed-trail-wildflower-nature-hike
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Not Loud Concerts Presents… Summer Sessions at Napa Yard
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T210000
UID:260524Zzv8vn4-TUaVMXR7siSf2w
DESCRIPTION:The Not Loud Concert folks are putting on 3 unique summer musi
 c festivals in Napa called Summer Sessions. The organizer of the event wou
 ld love to do an interview. Would it be possible to do an interview or an 
 article about what makes these summer music festivals unique?\n\nThese fes
 tivals are designed to be comfortable for both the musicians and the audie
 nce. Not Loud Concerts is attempting to break down all the bad stereotypes
  of music festivals. \n\nThey are called Summer Sessions and will be held
  at Napa Yard in Napa. Two bands will be on stage at the same time dueling
  it out and trading songs. \n\nThese music festivals will be from 7 - 9 p
 m\n\nBeer\, craft cocktails and BBQ will be available for purchase. \n\nE
 ach summer session has a different theme. \n\nJune 7 - Vintage Rock Night
  \n\nJuly 19 - Blues Night\n\nAug 16 - Country Boogie Night\n\nThis festi
 val is brought to you by Not Loud Concerts\, an organization that makes co
 ncerts a relaxing and fun experience by being “Not too long\, Not too ex
 pensive\, and Not too Loud.”
LOCATION:Napa Yard
URL:https://www.notloudconcerts.com/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
