BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T170000
UID:260508ZYmxBF0KBE-XOzJxgt1wgg
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sunday Swing Night at Hall of the Above
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T190000
UID:260504hjfV2gR5akCywpUNqygR9A
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the first Sunday of every month for SUNDAY SWING NI
 GHT at *Hall of the Above*\n\n🎷 Featuring a new-to-HOTA band\, The doRi
 aN Mode! 🎷\n\nThe doRiaN Mode explores the Great American Songbook as i
 t dishes up vintage jazz\, swinging R&B\, and soulful ballads\, from the s
 ounds of 1920s speakeasies and 1930s big-band swing to 1940s jump blues an
 d the rollicking R&B of Ruth Brown. Vocalist and bassist Dorian Bartley l
 eads this Petaluma-based acoustic quartet featuring Robby Elfman on piano/
 clarinet\, Peter Graves on sax\, and Tony Blake on drums. Whether they’
 re stomping at the Savoy in salute to Count Basie or paying homage to R&B 
 legend Etta James\, the doRiaN Mode brings elegance to classic American mu
 sic.\n\n💃🏻 Jasmine Worrell\, the Bay Area’s top swing dance instru
 ctor\, will offer a class from 4:15 – 5:00\n\n👯 Followed by live musi
 c and an open dance floor until 7:00 PM\n\n🎟️ $25 for admission inclu
 des the class — cash at the door. Kids 12 and under are free.\n\n🕺
 🏾 All skill levels welcome\; no partner required.\n\nSee you on the dan
 ce floor!
LOCATION:Hall of the Above
URL:https://www.halloftheabove.com/event-database/swing-dancing-at-hall-of
 -the-above-87jr4-tf756-m2l57-33xey-n2f47
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:COUNTRY CHORALE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T170000
UID:260430Sa4EAkz11kOjLibmWrN4mQ
DESCRIPTION:Sing Napa Valley Presents: COUNTRY CHORALE - A Choral Celebrat
 ion of Country Music\n\nGet ready for rich harmonies\, heartfelt storytell
 ing\, and “toes-tappin’” fun! Sing Napa Valley community choir invit
 es you to Country Chorale\, a lively and contemporary choral concert celeb
 rating the uniquely American tradition of country music.\n\nFrom Dolly Par
 ton and John Denver to Brandi Carlile\, Gram Parsons\, and The Chicks\, th
 is program features beloved country classics reimagined through glorious c
 horal harmony—performed by women’s\, men’s\, and mixed ensembles\, p
 lus our full choir. Whether you’re a lifelong country fan or just love g
 reat choral music\, Country Chorale offers something for everyone. Come en
 joy a fresh\, sophisticated take on a genre full of heart\, soul\, and har
 mony!\n\n📅 Sunday\, June 7\, 2026 🕒 3:00 p.m.\n\n📍 First Presbyte
 rian Church Gymnasium\,\n\n1333 Third Street\, downtown Napa \\(across fro
 m the Uptown Theatre\\)\n\n🎟 Tickets: $25 General Admission $10 Student
 s\n\n👉 Grab your tickets and join us for an afternoon of unforgettable 
 music!
LOCATION:First Presbyterian Church
URL:http://www.singnapavalley.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
