BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Sundays on the Plaza - Cabanijazz Project
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T170000
UID:260429ZJhy330DD0SxnevmN8i6NA
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nThis wee
 k's lineup features Cabanijazz Project! Javier Cabanillas is a Grammy-winn
 ing Mexican conga player\, composer\, and bandleader based in the San Fran
 cisco Bay Area. Cabanillas now leads Cabanijazz Project\, an electrifying 
 8-piece Latin ensemble performing original\, “hella” danceable music.\
 n\nSonoma Sundays are free and open to all\, thanks to the generous suppor
 t of the Sonoma Community Center\, The Dawn Redwoods Trust\, and the McNee
 ly Family Foundation.\n\nPack your picnic\, bring your dancing shoes\, and
  meet us on the Plaza!
LOCATION:Grinstead Amphitheater
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-6-7/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Redwood Connections at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T120000
UID:260429UiThsE1NPUaak_o0T0XDvQ
DESCRIPTION:Engage\, tune in\, and experience the forest in a whole new wa
 y with California Naturalist Laura Wagner.\n\nThis guided experience blend
 s hiking\, natural science\, sensory exploration\, and mindful reflection 
 as you make your way to the park’s ancient redwood\, a 2\,000-year-old g
 iant tucked into the slopes of Sonoma Mountain. Along the way\, you will p
 ause for interactive moments that engage your senses such as touch\, scent
 \, sound\, and sight\, opening new ways to experience the forest around yo
 u.\n\nThe outing features a moderately paced four-mile hike with approxima
 tely 620 feet of elevation gain. The experience concludes with a guided me
 ditation beneath the redwoods and a quiet\, reflective walk through the en
 chanting fairy ring forest.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/redwood-connections-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:American Red Cross Adult and Pediatric First-Aid/CPR/AED Class (Bl
 ended)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T134500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T161500
UID:260425e9MNInK7jUKgrKI6y572tQ
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to save a life!\n\nFocusing on recognizing and treat
 ing life-threatening situations in the critical minutes before 911 arrives
 \, we will cover how to handle adult and infant cardiac arrest\, choking\,
  heart attack\, severe bleeding and more!\n\nWe'll be using modern manikin
 s and equipment in a small-group setting\, answering questions along the w
 ay. Your American Red Cross certificate will be valid for 2 years.\n\nThis
  is a blended course: Watch the videos and presentations online at your ow
 n convenience before joining your patient and friendly instructor to pract
 ice your new skills!\n\n(This community class event is held at a branch of
  Sonoma County Library. We thank them for their hospitality. They have req
 uested that we mention that this program is neither sponsored by nor affil
