BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thursday Night Comedy - Kirk McHenry & Friends - Downtown Santa Ro
 sa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T220000
UID:260605-NoaqXDfJU6FqplkB2YG-A
DESCRIPTION:Thursday night stand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nStand
 -up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa VIP TABLES NOW AVAILABLE! Snag a table f
 or 4 with preferred seating\, your own private call button to summon servi
 ce\, and your first round of beer/cider (or a bottle of wine) for only $95
 !\n\nSpecial THURSDAY night show with KIRK MCHENRY & FRIENDS!\n\nMike Beta
 ncourt \, Carinne Salnave and Jose Contreras join Kirk for a hilarious nig
 ht out!\n\nMore about Kirk McHenry...\n\nA Splitting Comedy Style\n\nKirk 
 has the ability to deliver gut bursting laughs to his audience. This is wh
 at sets Kirk McHenry apart from the modern day comic. He has gained a lot 
 of knowledge because he was born and raised in Oakland\, California. This 
 knowledge comes from life in the inner city\, to prep school in the suburb
 s\, experiencing college life in the south and even a successful four-year
  stint in the Marine Corps.\n\nOpening for the Stars\n\nKirk blends all of
  his life experiences together into a story-telling brand of comedy due to
  the fact that he always views life through the eyes of a comic. Such come
 dy has been likened to Bill Cosby with a Richard Pryor twist. McHenry has 
 opened for comedic stars such as Paul Mooney\, Bobby Slayton\, Gary Owen\,
  and many more. Not to mention he’s opened for several musical acts incl
 uding KEM\, Tony Toni Tone\, The Whispers\, and Howard Hewitt. In turn\, K
 irk continues to leave audiences captivated across globe. Television Appea
 rances\n\nHis storytelling style of comedy is better than reality TV​. T
 his is because Kirk draws inspiration from everyday life. Kirk has had man
 y television appearances on BET’s Comic View\, One Mic Stand hosted by K
 evin Hart\, and Jamie Foxx’s Laffapalooza. He has also been talented eno
 ugh to be apart of several tours throughout the United States and abroad. 
 Notably\, this unforgettable comics’ voice can also be heard as the lead
  character of Toe Jam in the 2002 video game release of “Toe Jam & Earl 
 III: Mission to Earth.”\n\n21+ Doors - 7p / Show - 8p $15adv / $20door\n
 \nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahea
 d.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/thursday-night-comedy-kirk-mchenry-friend
 s-downtown-santa-rosa-tickets-1989403106244?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sister Act
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T220000
UID:260604NDgabYJtL02yreqmQEqxRA
DESCRIPTION:Sister Act is the high-energy musical comedy based on the belo
 ved 1992 film. Featuring an electrifying Alan Menken score infused with di
 sco and gospel beats\, this feel-good show is a celebration of music\, sis
 terhood\, and second chances. When disco diva Deloris Van Cartier witnesse
 s a crime\, she’s forced into hiding—in a convent! Disguised as a nun\
 , she transforms the struggling choir with her powerhouse voice\, helping 
 them find their sound while discovering her own. Nominated for five Tony A
 wards\, Sister Act is a joyful\, soul-stirring spectacle that proves music
 —and a little mischief—can work miracles
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/907119495682865/907119545682860/?activ
 e_tab=about
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
