BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Craft Pizza-Making Class Benefiting Sonoma Family Meal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T193000
UID:2605289MMejQi3x0af8kMG1VKMag
DESCRIPTION:Craft Pizza-Making Class with Chef Bryan Jones - June 11\n\n$1
 00.00\n\nWe’re finally bringing pizza to the Sonoma Family Meal kitchen!
  Join us and chef Bryan Jones for a cooking class on Thursday\, April 16th
  to learn how to perfect the art of scratch pizza dough\, marinara\, and m
 outhwatering toppings to satisfy all your senses.\n\nThe hands-on\, collab
 orative class will last 2.5 hours\, with time to enjoy your meal together 
 at the end. Whether you’re a seasoned cook or just starting out\, this c
 lass will offer a fun\, engaging learning environment\, while raising fund
 s for Sonoma Family Meal’s free culinary job training and food-security 
 programs.\n\nIf you haven’t been to the SFM Kitchen yet\, this class is 
 also the perfect chance to visit and experience where the magic takes plac
 e and how the work gets done.\n\nWHEN: Thursday June 11\, 5-7:30pm WHERE: 
 SFM community kitchen\, 1370A Redwood Way\, Petaluma\n\nTHE MENU:\n\nScrat
 ch Pizza Dough\n\nScratch Marinara Sauce\n\nMargherita Pizza\n\nHot Honey 
 & Pepperoni Pizza\n\nBig Seasonal Salad will be served\n\nBYOB: Bring Your
  Own Beverage\n\nIf you have a specific food allergy or have any questions
  about the menu\, please contact hannah@sonomafamilymeal.org.\n\nPLEASE WE
 AR CLOSE TOED SHOES TO ALL CLASSES\n\nABOUT THE CHEF:\n\nBryan Jones takes
  the art of restaurant quality cuisine outside of the traditional restaura
 nt kitchen and into evocative local spaces and intimate environments. Offe
 ring boutique catering and private chef services\, Bryan offers a culinary
  experience that’s creative\, custom and designed from scratch for each 
 menu and every singular occasion. \n\nAs a graduate of the California Cul
 inary Academy in San Francisco\, Bryan brings over 20 years of experience 
 in the kitchen to his craft. His approach to food reflects a diverse resta
 urants background\, showcasing bold\, clean flavors and influences from a 
 variety of cultures. \n\nAs the Executive Chef at St. Francis Winery\, Br
 yan was the creative force behind the highly rated food and wine pairing p
 rogram at the winery\, where it was Zagat recommended and voted \\#1 resta
 urant by OpenTable diners in 2013 and 2015. He joined St. Francis winery i
 n 2014 after ten years as Chef and General Manager of the fig cafe and win
 e bar\, the sister restaurant of the girl and the fig. He has cooked in lo
 cations around the world\, including Garmisch\, Germany\, Vail\, Colorado\
 , Santa Fe\, New Mexico and many other locations throughout the Bay Area.
  \n\nBryan uses this culinary history—and a natural curiosity for how e
 xperiences translate onto the palette—to create one-of-a-kind experience
 s in unique locations and private homes across Wine Country\, and beyond.
LOCATION:Sonoma Family Meal Community Kitchen
URL:https://www.sonomafamilymeal.org/store-2/craftpizza
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Different Expressions of Sonoma and Napa Cabernet Sauvignon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T200000
UID:2605282cyOvu_2bEec_S4KniW4aQ
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma Home Winemakers welcomes Chris Louton of St. Francis Wi
 nery on June 11 who will explore the differences between Sonoma vs. Napa C
 abernet Sauvignon.\n\nWith experience crafting luxury Cabernet in Napa bef
 ore joining St. Francis Winery in Sonoma Valley\, Louton will discuss why 
 Sonoma’s appellations and terroirs produce Bordeaux varietals with their
  own unique expression and intensity. Join us to learn why he calls Sonom
 a “a spectacular place to make Cabernet.”\n\n**Where:** Sonoma Commun
 ity Center -- Secret Garden\, next to the back parking lot\n\n**When:** D
 oors Open 6:30 PM | Talk 7:00 PM - 8:00PM\n\n**Cost:** Free\n\n**RSVP:**
  https://www.sonomahomewine.org/calendar\n\n**Note:**  21+ only| Bring 
 a glass for tasting and if you're a home winemaker a bottle to share
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center\, outside in the Secret Garden
URL:https://www.sonomahomewine.org/calendar
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Epicurean Adventures: Global Supper Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T213000
UID:260527WCsqnd5Wy06xdDAorcYv8w
DESCRIPTION:Experience an evening of bold flavors\, culture\, and collabor
 ation at Priest Ranch’s Global Supper Club. For this special installment
 \, our culinary team joins forces with Lafayette Chef JB Balingit of Hideo
 ut Kitchen and Tropa Modern Filipino to showcase the vibrant and soulful c
 uisine of the Philippines. Together\, they’ve crafted a thoughtfully cur
 ated menu that celebrates traditional Filipino dishes with a modern touch
 —each course expertly paired with Priest Ranch and Somerston Wines. From
  rich\, savory classics to bright\, layered flavors\, this immersive dinin
 g experience is designed to transport you\, bringing people together over 
 exceptional food\, wine\, and storytelling. Set in an intimate and welcomi
 ng atmosphere\, the Global Supper Club invites guests to explore new taste
 s\, connect with fellow diners\, and enjoy a truly memorable night at the 
 table.\n\n**What’s Included:**\n\nA multi-course\, family-style meal \n
 \nThoughtfully paired wines from Priest Ranch and Somerston Estate will be
  selected to enhance each dish\n\nA culinary takeaway showcasing their cul
 inary influences\n\nAnd access to exclusive pricing and limited-release bo
 ttles of the night’s featured wines\n\nJoin us for this exclusive dining
  experience\, blending global cuisines with the artistry of Napa Valley w
 ine. Seating is extremely limited\, so secure your place at the table for 
 this exciting evening!
LOCATION:Priest Ranch
URL:https://priestranchwines.com/events/epicurean-adventures-global-supper
 -club-06112026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
