BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Secret Lives of Mountain Lions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T200000
UID:260422Dmb24Cl0U0WKcbUyEWtIjQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an exciting evening as we explore the world of one
  of our most fascinating and elusive neighbors\, the mountain lion. Discov
 er how trail cameras are helping researchers track and study local mountai
 n lion populations\, providing key insights into their behavior and moveme
 nt.\n\nAs part of **California State Parks Week**\, https://castateparksw
 eek.org/\, take an educational evening hike (~3 miles roundtrip) with stop
 s along the way to learn about the four-legged residents that call the par
 k home. You will get an inside look at how researchers track mountain lion
 s\, study their behavior\, and gather data using trail cameras\, GPS colla
 rs\, and DNA samples.\n\nThe information collected through the Living with
  Lions project\, led by All Hands Ecology\, https://www.allhandsecology.or
 g/\,  in partnership with True Wild Conservation\, https://www.truewild.o
 rg/\,  is shared with the California Department of Fish and Wildlife\,  
 scientific journals\, local media\, and presented through engaging communi
 ty presentations.\n\nThis program offers a rare chance to understand the v
 ital role mountain lions play in maintaining a healthy ecosystem\, the sci
 ence behind the trail camera project\, and how our local community can hel
 p protect these incredible animals. Do not miss this opportunity to get up
  close with the research and meet the people making it possible.\n\nGuide 
 Kate Remsen has been working with All Hands Ecology’s Living with Lions 
 project as the Trail Camera Project Manager for 5 years. Her job includes 
 community outreach\, engagement\, and mountain lion research by placing an
 d servicing trail cameras on private properties in the Sonoma and Napa Val
 leys. Kate has a background in Film and Television Production and in 2019\
 , partnered with UC Davis’ Wildlife Health Center\, produced California
  Mountain Lions\, a 9-chapter docu-series on mountain lions in California
 . The series is being used for educational purposes by organizations such 
 as the Mountain Lion Foundation\, the National Wildlife Federation\, the 
 Institute for Wildlife Studies\, and many more\, helping to shed light on 
 the conflicts mountain lions face in California.\n\n**California State Pa
 rks Week** is presented jointly by **California State Parks**\, **Save 
 the Redwoods League**\, **Parks California**\, and **California State Pa
 rks Foundation.**
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/mountain-lions/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T193000
UID:260415Cy0__1UxDEubTAent8TsNA
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Napa Valley Jazz Getaway
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T000000
UID:260327kef86rrG4ku05tx5xrwABA
DESCRIPTION:Jonathan is the product of the Western World. \n\n At thirteen
 \, Jonathan's talents caught the ears and eyes of British record producer 
 Clive Caulder. He was signed to Caulder's Jive Records and as the old clic
 he goes\, the rest is history. \n\n \n\n Jonathan's first single broke dow
 n racial barriers\, becoming the first song by a black artist to be played
  by white radio stations in South Africa. Because Jive was headquartered i
 n England\, Jonathan decided to move there to focus on his recording caree
 r. His commitment to his craft paid off with his self-titled debut album\,
  which received a Grammy nomination for the pop hit &quot\;Lies.&quot\; \n
 \n \n\n Jonathan's ability to blend his roots in African music with wester
 n pop sensibilities would be a trademark of many albums to follow\, though
  never more refined than in his latest release. \n\n \n\n For example\, th
 e first single from Jonathan is a rendition of the folk-rock classic &quot
 \;Fire and Rain.&quot\; Butler breathes new life into this classic\, infus
 ing the vocals with intensity\, as subtle as it is powerful. The musical a
 rrangement is lively and soulful\, indicative of his roots in World music.
  &quot\;Fire and Rain&quot\; is already garnering accolades from top radio
  programmers. Lori Lewis\, program director for WSMJ in Baltimore states\,
  &quot\;It literally gave me a lump in my throat. I walked into the studio
  and introduced it live on air. Vocals this great are really rare.&quot\;
LOCATION:Blue Note Summer Sessions at Meritage Resort
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107690478?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T000000
UID:260224XkdICWWNUEWQYtXinHIpLA
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Iron & Vine Restaurant Bar & Events
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107935760?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dave Sampson Music & The Sorentinos
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T000000
UID:260224WWGC2fSwyUODiCBpKyiQLA
DESCRIPTION:Based in the San Francisco Bay Area\, Dave Sampson is a freela
 nce guitarist\, producer\, multi-instrumtentalist and music instructor. Dr
 awing from his experiences living and playing in the music scenes of Austi
 n\, Los Angeles\, Seattle\, and Memphis\, Sampson put roots down in the Ba
 y Area in 2004. Dave's vibrant and versatile style supports a wide range o
 f genres and artists. His work can be heard on a variety of records\, majo
 r films\, and national radio and television shows. Always favoring taste\,
  melody\, and finding the perfect complimentary part\, his approach to pla
 ying has been compared to Mike Campbell\, David Lindley\, Mark Knopfler\, 
 Daniel Lanois and Lindsey Buckingham.
LOCATION:The Saloon at The Jack London Lodge
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107917982?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
