BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We Rise With Pride Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T220000
UID:260508hTbFhgU4l0e5X03lHRCOhQ
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for Sonoma Valley Pride kickoff concert!\n\nJ. Grave
 s\, band and Drag Artists Kochina Rude\, and Tila Pia\, will take the stag
 e with high energy rock n roll and drag performances.  Hosted by the histo
 ric Sebastiani Theater\, this event will launch a weekend of PRIDE!\n\nThi
 s first annual concert is also a frundraiser for Sonoma Valley Pride\, whi
 ch helps support future events and programming in Sonoma Valley.\n\nCome r
 eady to party!Doors open at 7:15 for an 8:00 show time. Wine will be avail
 able for purchase at the venue.\n\nSee more about the artists below. J. Gr
 aves\n\nJ. Graves is a Portland based\, queer non binary led dance punk pr
 oject blending angularguitar work\, pounding rhythms\, and resolute vocals
  into an infectious\, high energy sound.For fans of The Kills\, Yeah Yeah 
 Yeahs\, and Metric\, the project sits at the crossroads of postpunk intens
 ity and dance floor release.The single &ldquo\;South Pole&rdquo\; was rele
 ased alongside an NPR Tiny Desk On the Road tourperformance. Past releases
  include Undercover Summer\, a cover series reimaginingDepeche Mode\, Devo
 \, and Blondie\, and Fortress of Fun\, a choose your own adventure LP.In 2
 026\, J. Graves is releasing a new full length record while expanding fest
 ivalappearances and international reach\, anchored by a live show known fo
 r its connection\,movement\, and impact.\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nKochina Rude - Drag Artist &l
 dquo\;The Narcan Queen&rdquo\; Kochina Rude is a drag queen\, ex-vocalist 
 of post-punk band Lolly Gaggers\, and internationally recognized harm redu
 ction advocate based in the Bay Area. Armed with a hard femme aesthetic\, 
 &ldquo\;do-it-yourself&rdquo\; attitude\, and over a decade of experience 
 in Bay Area nightlife\, Kochina's work blends activism and drag in her rol
 e as an artist and emcee.\n\nTila Pia - Drag Artist - 
LOCATION:Sebastiani Theatre
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/we-rise-with-pride-concert
 ?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
