BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack London Speaker Series: Tarnel Abbott - Jack's Great Granddaug
 hter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T120000
UID:260513SAiMSssqu0moMPgBjEECiQ
DESCRIPTION:Jack London’s great-granddaughter Tarnel Abbott will speak i
 n an interview format presentation. A retired librarian who spent 22 years
  at the Richmond Public Library\, Abbott has dedicated herself to preservi
 ng London’s books and papers. She is also a longtime activist\, involved
  in numerous local and international causes\, and will share her insights 
 into London’s life and legacy.\n\nShe will be interviewed by Gail Yamamo
 to Seymour\, an environmental scientist and advocate for endangered specie
 s\, climate change adaptation\, and environmental justice. She is a third 
 generation Californian Japanese American.  Over the past 50 years\, Seymo
 ur has been a self-educated follower of Jack London’s history\, drawn to
  his adventurous lifestyle and humanitarian ideologies.  Gail treasures h
 er friendship with Tarnel Abbott\, Jack London’s great granddaughter\, b
 ecause like her great grandfather and grandmother\, she is genuinely compa
 ssionate and is a vocal activist promoting justice for all.\n\nThis is par
 t of a quarterly speaker series\, co-presented by the Jack London Society 
 and Jack London Park Partners\, in honor of Jack London’s 150th birthday
  year.  The series features a range of experts and scholars\, sharing ins
 ights into Jack London’s life\, work\, and legacy and his connections to
  literature\, photography\, and the Bay Area.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/jl-speaker-series-tarnel-abbott/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Made Local Marketplace Watercolor Painting: Punch the Baby Monkey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T130000
UID:260511wTDzj8EOw0yzmjgD8Qquww
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a creative\, family-friendly morning at Montgomery Villa
 ge with a guided watercolor workshop led by local artist Irina Miller. Thi
 s thoughtfully designed class invites guests of all ages to explore the fu
 ndamentals of watercolor while creating a charming baby monkey painting to
  take home.\n\nDesigned with beginners in mind\, the experience offers ste
 p-by-step instruction in a relaxed\, welcoming setting — perfect for ind
 ividuals\, families\, or anyone looking to try something new.\n\nDuring th
 e workshop\, guests will:\n\nLearn foundational watercolor techniques\n\nF
 ollow guided\, step-by-step instruction\n\nComplete a finished painting to
  take home\n\nAll materials and tools are provided.\n\nDetails: $45 per pe
 rson 2-hour session Maximum of 20 participants\n\nAdvance registration is 
 required. Workshops are held outdoors (undercover) at Made Local Marketpla
 ce. Space is limited\, with a minimum of four participants required. A min
 imum of 72 hours’ notice is needed for partial refunds.
LOCATION:Made Local at Montgomery Village
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/made-local-marketplace-watercolo
 r-painting-punch-the-baby-monkey/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
