DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T203000
UID:260511sM48m8scsEWazVu8sFoyLQ
DESCRIPTION:The Laugh Cellar presents: Headliner Comedian Cathy Ladman at 
 DeLoach Vineyards\n\nCathy Ladman is an award-winning stand-up comedian\, 
 writer\, and actress. She has appeared on *The Tonight Show* 10 times\, wi
 th Jimmy Fallon\, Jay Leno\, and Johnny Carson\, including the final two a
 nniversary shows of Johnny Carson’s *Tonight Show*. She has also appeare
 d six times on *The Late Late Show with Craig Ferguson*\, had her own HBO 
 *One Night Stand* special\, a Showtime special\, and numerous other televi
 sion comedy appearances. In addition\, she was a writer for the hit televi
 sion shows *Roseanne* and *Caroline in the City*.\n\nComplimentary parking
  on-site\n\nOutdoor event \n\nDoors 6:00pm  / Showtime 7:00pm\n\nAVAILAB
 LE FOR PURCHASE: \n\nA beautiful selection of wine and sparkling wine \n
 \nOakville Cheese & Charcuterie trays\n\n21+ Event
LOCATION:DeLoach Vineyards
URL:https://www.crushersofcomedy.com/june132026.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Second Saturday Cartoonist: Mara Ramirez
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T150000
UID:260511VWkHAuwbVUGPfw17tMwFOg
DESCRIPTION:Meet\, watch\, and talk to Ignatz-nominated interdisciplinary 
 artist and educator **Mara Ramirez**\, whose work ruminates on the body i
 n space through metaphor\, fantasy\, and realism alike. Bending images of 
 biological life\, the stories they tell range in content\, from poetic med
 itations on gender to funny and sad character studies in cartoon formats. 
 Ramirez is the creator of *Flea* (2025 Fieldmouse Press)\, as well as ma
 ny short runs of poetry comics from Floss Editions\, Irrelevant Press\, an
 d (self-published) Freak Comics.\n\nA lifelong zinester and Esnupi lover\,
  Ramirez will be sharing a make-your-own mini-zine project!
LOCATION:Charles M. Schulz Museum
URL:https://schulzmuseum.org/mara-ramirez/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SugarShuttle: Sugarloaf ↔ Hood Mtn\, Pythian Rd-CA State Parks W
 eek
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T110000
UID:2605115NWbMfP5VUyjR0JuT9UtHw
DESCRIPTION:How it works: Every half hour\, our Shuttle will leav
 e from either Sugarloaf Ridge State Park's Visitor Center \\(maki
 ng a brief stop at the Goodspeed parking lot\\) or Hood Mountai
 n Regional Park’s Pythian Rd parking lot \\(with a brief stop
  at the equestrian lot\\). Make a reservation to ride to the o
 ther end of the trail and begin your hike\, or hike and ride 
 back. We recommend riding first and hiking back to your car aft
 erward– no worries about how long you take to finish your adv
 enture. The hike should take 3½ to 4½ hours\; the distance is
  about 7.4 miles one-way with approximately 2\,300ft of elevation
  gain. Bring at least 64 oz of water and sun protection\, as 
 the majority of the trail is exposed. \n\nIf you are riding fro
 m Sugarloaf\, the Goodspeed lot fills up quickly. If it is full
 \, please park at the main lot and pick up the shuttle at the
  Visitor Center \\(you will have to hike a mile back to the m
 ain lot from the bottom of the canyon/Goodspeed lot\\). If the 
 Hood Mt. Pythian Lot is full\, please park at the Equestrian Lo
 t\, by the Hood House\, in Los Guilicos. \n\nRegistration is req
 uired as there is only space for 5 riders at a time\, but you
  can ride on a space-available basis as well. There is no char
 ge for the ride\, the $10 reservation fee is refunded on site 
 the day of the event\, unless you choose to donate it to keep
  this service running. Dogs and bikes are not allowed in the s
 huttle or on Goodspeed Trail \\(the State Park portion of the h
 iking route\\). Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026spwk-satshuttle
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
