BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What is a Print
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T200000
UID:260607lW7oP7DS5EyF_gqSOs3dxQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18 and over\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nWhat is a Print? A lively\, i
 llustrated presentation introducing Printmaking with Linda Goodman. Discov
 er how original prints are made&mdash\;and how to tell them apart from rep
 roductions. You will learn about key techniques \\(etching\, woodcut\, lit
 hography\, silkscreen\\)\, plus monoprints\, gicl&eacute\;e\, art prints\,
  editions\, and what &ldquo\;unique&rdquo\; vs. &ldquo\;multiple&rdquo\; p
 rints mean. See real tools\, plates\, and sample prints up close. Bring a 
 print you own for identification if time allows. Questions welcome.\n\nThi
 s class is located in the Main Gallery.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nLinda Go
 odman is a Petaluma-based painter and printmaker known for her pioneering 
 work in monotype. She holds an MFA in Printmaking from Mills College and a
  BA from Stanford University\, where she studied with Nathan Oliveira. Her
  work is included in major collections such as the Brooklyn Museum and the
  Library of Congress. An experienced educator\, she has taught widely in t
 he U.S. and abroad and now teaches from her Petaluma studio\, while also c
 ontributing as a curator\, juror\, and arts writer.\n\nLearn more about Li
 nda! \n\nwww.artmondo.com@lindagoodmanart
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-what-is-a-print
 ?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drawing a Clothed Figure
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T210000
UID:260607WGdMucNwSU-NX5EyFTT5dA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nEver tried drawing a human figure and ended up with some
 thing that looks like a coat rack in sweatpants? You're not alone. In this
  lighthearted workshop\, we'll tackle the clothed figure&mdash\;those myst
 erious folds\, wrinkles\, and gravity-defying hoodies&mdash\;while keeping
  things fun and approachable. Learn how fabric actually behaves \\(spoiler
 : it has opinions\\)\, how it drapes over the body\, and how to suggest fo
 rm without drawing every single wrinkle like a laundry catalog. Through gu
 ided exercises and plenty of laughs\, you'll build confidence\, sharpen yo
 ur observation skills\, and finally make peace with sleeves\, pants\, and 
 that one jacket that never looks right. All skill levels welcome&mdash\;ye
 s\, even if your last figure drawing wore three left shoes.\n\nThis worksh
 op is located in the classroom.\n\nStudents bring: \n\nFavorite drawing pa
 d and pencils\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nCharles &ldquo\;Chuck&rdquo\; Pyle
  is a lifelong artist and painter-illustrator whose career began in 1976. 
 He's known for storytelling work that blends humor and drama while delight
 ing clients and collectors. He received the Distinguished Educator in the 
 Arts Award from the Society of Illustrators and an honorary doctorate from
  the Academy of Art University\, where he served for many years as Chair o
 f the School of Illustration before retiring in 2021. He is also a foundin
 g artist member of the Sonoma and Telluride Plein Air groups and has exhib
 ited widely. \n\nLearn more about Chuck: \n\nwww.charlespyle.net\n\n@chuck
 pyle
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-drawing-clothe
 d-person?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stitch Your Story: Soft Sculpture Self-Portraits
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T160000
UID:2606071GhXsaS1KU-CWYscGhDbLQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 10\\+\n\nIn this workshop\, students will explore and celebrate t
 heir identity\, interests\, and personal expression through art. They will
  create their own unique soft sculpture portrait\, and experience creative
  skill-building as they draw and paint on fabric and hand-sew their finish
 ed piece. \n\nThis workshop is located in the classroom.\n\nAbout the Teac
 her: \n\nAnn Ledo-Lane is an interdisciplinary artist\, educator and joycr
 after. Born in the Bay Area\, and currently living in a little redwood for
 est in Marin\, she focuses on cultivating joy through daily creative pract
 ices that intersect nature\, memory\, and the everyday. A long-time creati
 ve educator in arts-centered public schools\, Ann is delighted to engage i
 n artistic play through pop up arts workshops\, community arts spaces\, an
 d on the college level\, ensuring creative practices are accessible to man
 y and a tool for equity\, personal wellness\, and connection. Ann lives wi
 th her two children\, dog\, and husband\, sculptor\, Sebastian Lane\, who 
 all share her love of outdoor adventuring\, making\, and chair design.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-stitch-your-st
 ory?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Art Playground
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T160000
UID:2606041XvQuBxGkkW3pkTIqYkhig
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nDive into the world of digital art without the steep lea
 rning curve! This course is a creative playground designed for curious min
 ds of all ages. We're ditching the complex technical jargon and focusing p
 urely on experimentation\, play\, and discovery. You'll get hands-on exper
 ience with a diverse suite of accessible\, easy-to-use software to bring y
 our imagination to life. Go from sketching your first digital illustration
 s to sculpting beginner-friendly 3D models and bringing characters to life
  with simple animation. Bring your curiosity\, jump in\, and let's make so
 me art!\n\nThis class is located in the Main Gallery. \n\nStudents bring:\
 n\nLaptops\n\nPAC provides: \n\nExtension Chords\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\
 nLije Morgan teaches animation\, 3D\, and game design\, and offers private
  lessons for artists exploring new media. Their work examines the power of
  &ldquo\;cute&rdquo\; aesthetics as tools of persuasion and subversion\, o
 ften blending 2D and 3D techniques using Blender. Passionate about storyte
 lling through games and animation\, Lije also creates live visuals for per
 formances and hosts Boiled Over\, a podcast featuring independent animator
 s from around the world.\n\nLearn more: \n\nwww.lije.com@lije.mo
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-digital-art-pl
 ayground?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Tide to Treasure: Creating Wind Chimes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T120000
UID:260528sIcZ6QNzQUie6xCdQwT_CQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 10\\+\n\nDiscover where art\, science\, and the natural world mee
 t in this hands-on workshop inspired by the oyster-rich landscapes of West
  Marin. Through close observation and creative exploration\, participants 
 will have the opportunity to explore cultural and ecological stories while
  transforming locally gathered driftwood\, oyster shells\, and natural mat
 erials into a wind chime or wall hanging. Blending art with natural histor
 y\, this class invites you to slow down\, look closely\, and create a mean
 ingful piece that echoes the textures\, rhythms\, and stories of the coast
 .\n\nThis workshop is located in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\
 nSue Dedina is an experienced Interpretive Educator who has taught for CA 
 State Parks\, US Forest Service\, Point Reyes National Seashore Associatio
 n and museums. With a BS in Marine Biology and studies in art\, she seeks 
 to bring the worlds of science and art together. Sue is a working artist w
 ith a studio at Novato Arts Center.\n\nLauren Volk has an MFA from Otis Co
 llage of Art and Design\, and a BFA from Art Center College of Design. She
  is a professional artist who teaches throughout the Bay Area. She is owne
 r of LVolkart Studio in Novato where she teaches private workshops and cla
 sses associated with the Marin Museum of Contemporary Art. She has also be
 en awarded multiple teaching awards from Art Center College of Design.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-tide-to-treasu
 re?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
