BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Preparing an Art Portfolio: A Workshop for Teens and their Parents
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260616T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260616T200000
UID:260528W2EIWidUcUqtrXF9Joekgg
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 14-19\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nIs your teen thinking about applyin
 g to art school or a college with an art program? Ever wondered what you s
 hould include or what pitfalls to avoid? In this workshop\, portfolio coac
 h and educator Barbara Pollak shows some case studies and general tips for
  making your work stand out and\, more importantly\, tell your story. This
  dynamic course is designed for high school students ready to elevate thei
 r artwork and stand out in the college application process.\n\nQ &amp\; A 
 to follow. Parents are welcome. \n\nThis class is located in the Main Gall
 ery.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nBarbara Pollak is a San Francisco&ndash\;ba
 sed fine artist\, curator\, and arts educator who specializes in helping t
 weens and teens develop strong\, concept-driven art portfolios. Since 2016
 \, she has focused on fostering creative exploration and personal vision t
 hrough her teaching. She has taught Pre-College Drawing and Illustration a
 nd Atelier classes at the California College of the Arts\, along with priv
 ate workshops in figure drawing and painting. She holds a BFA in Animation
 /Film from the Rhode Island School of Design and an MA in Arts Education f
 rom Boston University.\n\nLearn more about Barbara! \\(Below are photos of
  student artwork\\)\n\nwww.freckleshop.com@happypixart
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-teen-art-portfo
 lios?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
