BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zines for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T160000
UID:260607D0S2KVUHrEm2I8lLNOiEwA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13-19\n\nJump into a high-energy\, hands-on zine-making experienc
 e where teens bring their ideas to life through bold visuals and DIY story
 telling. Using hand-drawing\, collage\, found papers\, and simple binding 
 techniques\, participants create their own self-published mini magazines f
 rom start to finish. Whether the message is political\, personal\, social\
 , or playful\, this workshop empowers creative voices to be seen and share
 d&mdash\;resulting in a one-of-a-kind zine that's as expressive and unique
  as its maker.\n\nThis class is located in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Te
 acher: \n\nAnn Ledo-Lane is an interdisciplinary artist\, educator and joy
 crafter. Born in the Bay Area\, and currently living in a little redwood f
 orest in Marin\, she focuses on cultivating joy through daily creative pra
 ctices that intersect nature\, memory\, and the everyday. A long-time crea
 tive educator in arts-centered public schools\, Ann is delighted to engage
  in artistic play through pop up arts workshops\, community arts spaces\, 
 and on the college level\, ensuring creative practices are accessible to m
 any and a tool for equity\, personal wellness\, and connection. Ann lives 
 with her two children\, dog\, and husband\, sculptor\, Sebastian Lane\, wh
 o all share her love of outdoor adventuring\, making\, and chair design.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-zines-for-teens
 ?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Tools in Painting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T120000
UID:2606077Oc4w4NfjkSnvqwfWWnLaA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nTake your traditional painting skills to the next level 
 by harnessing the power of digital tools you already own. In this useful w
 orkshop\, you'll learn how to transform your own photographs into polished
  watercolor\, gouache\, or oil paintings using mobile devices\, tablets\, 
 and intuitive apps for gridding\, color matching\, and design. Drawing on 
 techniques used that Gorsiski developed for top studios like Walt Disney a
 nd Industrial Light &amp\; Magic\, this class shows how technology can sim
 plify complex processes\, improve accuracy\, and speed up execution. This 
 will help you create more confident\, professional-level work from start t
 o finish.\n\nThis class is located in the classroom. \n\nStudent brings: \
 n\nCharged iPad and Pencil\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nGregory Gorsiski is a
  digital artist\, animator\, and video game designer with over 35 years of
  experience in the entertainment industry. His career has included work wi
 th major studios such as Walt Disney Television\, Industrial Light &amp\; 
 Magic\, and Electronic Arts\, as well as leading his own production compan
 y\, Artysta Studios\, since 1985. Now retired from the digital industry\, 
 Gregory is dedicating his time to traditional art\, bringing decades of cr
 eative experience to a new chapter at the easel.\n\nLearn more about Grego
 ry: \n\nwww.artysta.studio
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-digital-toolsp
 aint?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sculpture Uncovered: A Survey of Materials & Methods
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T200000
UID:2606076SjFLzcVuUmnJ8cbMquxnA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13 and over\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nThis presentation offers a su
 rvey of sculptural practice across a range of materials and techniques. Fr
 om traditional processes like carving and casting to contemporary approach
 es using mixed media and found objects\, the talk explores how artists thi
 nk in three dimensions and bring form to life. Through visual examples and
  clear explanations\, participants will gain insight into the possibilitie
 s of sculpture and the diverse ways artists approach making. Ideal for any
 one curious about the language of form\, material\, and space.\n\nThis cla
 ss is located in the Main Gallery.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-sculpture-surve
 y?aff=cityspark
