BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Secret Garden the Musical
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T220000
UID:260606mz_eQt4VYUCQImGvO73I3w
DESCRIPTION:Step into a world of wonder\, mystery\, and renewal.\n\nCinnab
 ar Theater presents The Secret Garden The Musical\, the beloved story brou
 ght to life with a soaring score and breathtaking storytelling.\n\nOrphane
 d and sent to live with her reclusive uncle in a grand English manor\, you
 ng Mary Lennox discovers a hidden\, neglected garden. As she nurtures it b
 ack to life\, she awakens something magical—not only in the world around
  her\, but in the hearts of those who have long been closed off to hope.\n
 \nThis enchanting adaptation by Marsha Norman and Lucy Simon\, based on th
 e classic novel by Frances Hodgson Burnett\, is a moving tale of healing\,
  transformation\, and the power of nature.\n\n**Performance Dates & Times:
 **\n\nJune 12–June 28\, 2026\n\nFridays at 7:30 PM\n\nSaturdays at 7:30 
 PM\n\nSundays at 2:00 PM\n\nLearn more at cinnabartheater.org\n\n**Locatio
 n:**\n\nSonoma State University – Warren Theater (Ives Hall)\n\n1801 Eas
 t Cotati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA 94928\n\nRun Time:\n\nApproximately 2 hou
 rs 30 minutes\, including one 15-minute intermission\n\nRecommended For:\n
 \nAppropriate for all ages – perfect for families\n\n⸻\n\nCast:\n\nMar
 y Lennox: Violet Spears\n\nAlternate Mary Lennox: Serena Ridout\n\nColin C
 raven: Nathanael Koross\n\nAlternate Colin Craven: Joe Schulze\n\nArchibal
 d Craven: Ben Sasnett\n\nLily: Syona Ayyankeril\n\nRose / Dreamer: Katie V
 eale\n\nMartha: Nicole Stanley\n\nMrs. Medlock: Tika Moon\n\nBen Weatherst
 aff: Jonathan Spencer\n\nDickon: Beckett Hepp\n\nClaire / Dreamer: Natalie
  Burton\n\nAlice / Dreamer: Miriam Valencia\n\nMrs. Winthrop / Dreamer: Ka
 thi Brotemarkle\n\nAlbert / Dreamer: David A. Bradbury\n\nMajor Holmes & S
 helly / Dreamer: Noah Evans\n\nLt. Shaw / Dreamer: Corey Wilson\n\nLt. Wri
 ght / Dreamer: Mason Hunt\n\nNeville Craven: Zachary Hasbany\n\n⸻\n\nCre
 ative Team:\n\nJane Erwin: Director\n\nBrett Strader: Music Director\n\nBr
 idget Codoni: Choreographer\n\nElise Clark: Stage Manager\n\nJohn Sheridan
 : Assistant Stage Manager\n\nRoss Tiffany-Brown: Technical Director\n\nApr
 il George: Lighting Designer\n\nMateo Felix: Prop Designer / Co-Sound Desi
 gner\n\nDonnie Frank: Costume Designer & Hair/Makeup Designer\n\nPeter Cro
 mpton: Set Designer\n\nJohn Rustan: Dialect Coach\n\nLaurynn Malilay: Co-S
 ound Designer\n\nDiane Dragone: Executive Director\n\nNathan Cummings: Art
 istic Director\n\n⸻\n\nGetting to Sonoma State University:\n\nThe Warren
  Theater is located in Ives Hall on the Sonoma State University campus in 
 Rohnert Park. Plan to arrive early to allow time for parking and walking t
 o the venue.\n\nhttps://cinnabartheater.org/show/thesecretgarden/
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Warren Theater\, Located in Ives Hall
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/thesecretgarden/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society’s Seminar
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T160000
UID:260605_r5JCjNrgEyC3yAnSJlBBA
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society Seminar\n\n With Lisa 
 Gorrell and Cindy Brennan\n\nHow to Develop a Research Plan with Lisa Gorr
 ell\n\nFinding your Railroad Ties with Cindy Brennan\n\n Saturday\, June 
 20th\n\n FREE\n\n 1:00pm—4:00pm PDT\n\n Virtual via Zoom login beginn
 ing at 12:30 p.m.\n\nIn person come by noon and enjoy some light refreshme
 nts\n\n **1:00-2:00 How to Develop a Research Plan with Lisa Gorrell**\n\
 n Do you feel like your research results go in circles\, that you keep fin
 ding the same information\, or you have brick walls you cannot solve? Lisa
  will explain how to create and use a research plan which will keep you fo
 cused on your research.\n\n Lisa S. Gorrell is a Certified Genealogist an
 d has served on boards of several genealogical societies including the Son
 oma County Genealogical Society.\n\n **2:00-2:30 Interactive Break**\n\n
  **2:30-3:30 Finding your Railroad Ties with Cindy Brennan**\n\n There a
 re only a few things that are as entwined with American history as the Rai
 lroad. For many of our ancestors\, trains represented the most profound ch
 ange in their lifetime. New careers\, travel\, food\, medicine and product
 s that were never available before\, were now a possibility. Join us on a 
 virtual train trip to learn how your family was connected to the magic of 
 the Railroad.\n\n Cindy Brennan has been an avid family history researche
 r for over 20 years. Since 2009\, she has served as the editor of the Sono
 ma County Genealogy Society's monthly newsletter.  \n\n This meeting is
  held in-person at the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints in the 
 Cultural Hall\, 1725 Peterson Lane\, Santa Rosa or you can attend via Zoom
 .\n\n Even if you are attending in person you must register at **https://
 www.scgsonline.org**\n\n Registration closes Friday\, June 19th
LOCATION:Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints 
URL:https://www.scgsonline.org 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plein Air Watercolor Landscapes: A Day at Jack London Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T150000
UID:260605TDaweCsez0qVfQNcyR2NEQ
DESCRIPTION:Spend a day immersed in plein air watercolor landscape paintin
 g while taking in the sweeping vistas of Jack London State Historic Park.
  Participants will explore both watercolor technique and the core principl
 es of landscape painting\, including composition\, color temperature\, and
  atmospheric perspective. Learn to create movement and depth in your paint
 ing\, and gain a new appreciation for the beauty of your surroundings thro
 ugh the process of close observation and careful rendering.\n\nWe’ll sta
 rt the class with quick thumbnail sketches\, then select one composition t
 o focus on throughout the day. Through demonstration and individual instru
 ction\, you’ll learn color mixing and watercolor technique while buildin
 g your painting step by step.\n\nBring a picnic lunch to enjoy while takin
 g a break\, and a lightweight folding chair if you have one. Otherwise sea
 ting is at picnic tables and park benches or on the ground. All other mate
 rials are provided.\n\nAfter the workshop\, you’re invited to continue e
 xploring the park—take a hike\, visit the museum\, or stroll to the evoc
 ative ruins of the Wolf House.\n\nAll levels of experience are welcome!\n\
 nFor pricing information or to register for this class visit https://sonom
 acommunitycenter.org/programs/plein-air-watercolor-landscapes-a-day-at-jac
 k-london-park/.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/plein-air-watercolor-landscapes-june
 -2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
