DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T113000
UID:260523yr-GlpO4V0iY0NKfNQGEww
DESCRIPTION:**Long-Time Residents Tell Tales from 1976**\n\nHear about our
  town 50 years ago from a few people who remember it well. Joanne Taeuffer
  will interview long-time residents who share their memories of the econom
 ic and business environment\, the changes in the wine industry\, the found
 ation of the Healdsburg Museum and Historical Society\, the high school ba
 nd and more. And then we’ll ask audience members to tell their stories f
 rom 1976.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lavender Bloom Fest Open Farm Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T160000
UID:260523VO_U3GPqYE2Q4zytHFcdiA
DESCRIPTION:Mid-May to mid-July is the time when all the lavender at Bees 
 N Blooms is blooming with bright purple radiance\, and we open the farm to
  the public for Lavender Bloom Fest!\n\n**Lavender Bloom Fest Field Days:*
 * May 23\, May 30-31\, June 6-7\, June 13-14\, June 20\,\n\n**Lavender Su
 nset Evenings:** May\, 29\, June 5\, June 12\, June 19\, June 26\n\n**Jaz
 z Days:** May 24\, June 21\, and July 12\n\n**Lavender U-Cut Experience:*
 * June 27-28\, July 4-5\, July 11. Note: July 12 is also a U-Cut day\, bu
 t is listed under Jazz Days.\n\nBring the kids\, visit the poultry palace\
 , play farm bingo\, and snap a picture in the giant lavender chair! Shop t
 he Farm Stand and visit the Bees N Blooms Nursery. Sunset evenings are spe
 cial at Bees N Blooms. Enjoy the view as the suns shines a golden light on
  the lavender. Enjoy dinner with Tacos don Pepe\, then head to the labyrin
 th to watch the sunset.
LOCATION:Bees N Blooms
URL:https://beesnblooms.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:E. Live and Chesta Blake with Velvet Shadows and gamayabreak
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T220000
UID:260521_8iOHITEVUm3Ctqz260ufw
DESCRIPTION:Live music at Brooks Note Winery featuring E. Live and Chesta 
 Blake\, Velvet Shadows\, and DJ gamayabreak.\n\nE. Live and Chesta Blake 
 are a retro-styled dance duo playing original music from their vinyl rele
 ases on Star Creature Records\, along with creative new takes on 80's clas
 sics. \n\nVelvet Shadows are long-time friends that formed to make fun\,
  funky versions of their soul favorites. Chelsea handles vocals and bass a
 nd Eli plays guitar\, drums\, and produces. \n\nDJ gamayabreak is a Sant
 a Rosa based DJ who plays an eclectic mix of psych\, afrobeat\, brazillian
 \, jazz\, funk\, and disco exclusively on vinyl. He has performed locally 
 at Bloodroot Winery\, Shady Oak Brewing\, and is a regular in the rotation
  of djs at Glitter and Goth\, a monthly dance club in Santa Rosa.
LOCATION:Brooks Note Winery
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/e-live-and-chesta-blake
 -with-velvet-shadows-and-gamayabreak/18969049/2026-06-20T18
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Midsummer's Journey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T160000
UID:260519hUPg2WFlx0iTjKF8A4CpKg
DESCRIPTION:**WHAT: A Midsummer’s Journey – Oddities Market**\n\n **WH
 EN:  Saturday\, June 20th. 2026 10 am – 4 pm**\n\n **WHERE**: Soap Ca
 uldron/ Three Sisters Apothecary and garden\n\n11830 Main St.\, Penngrove\
 , CA 94951\n\n **Free event**\n\n **Special info:** Vendor participation 
 and performers will be provided in collaboration with the Menagerie & Oddi
 ties Expo.\n\n **Take A Midsummer’s Journey in Penngrove -  June 20**
  \n\n Join A Midsummer’s Journey and ODDventure to celebrate the Summer
  Solstice at Soap Cauldron on June 20 from 10 am to 4 pm at Three Sisters 
 Apothecary and garden in Penngrove. \n\n Step into an immersive midsumme
 r bazaar of wonder that blends artisan craftsmanship\, whimsical performan
 ce\, interactive ritual\, and community discovery. \n\n Guests are invit
 ed to wander\, explore\, and delight in curious\, magical\, and adventurou
 s encounters along the way. Designed as a welcoming\, come-and-go gatherin
 g\, Guests may participate as deeply or lightly as they wish.\n\n Through
 out the day\, you will encounter (sample of activities): \n\nOpening Jour
 ney Invocation\n\nInsect Pinning Workshop\n\nDragon-Tail Performance\n\nAl
 tar of Roads (honoring origins\, crossroads\, & new journeys)\n\nWhimsical
  Roaming Creatures\n\nOracles of the Crossroads\n\nA Wayfarer’s Gift Raf
 fle\n\nTraveler Portrait Experience\n\nFirst-Arrival Journey Totes\n\nComp
 limentary Midsummer Provisions\n\nSilk\, a whimsical roaming character\n\n
 Featured Musical Performance by Aursjoen: AURSJOEN\n\n More details:\n\n
 Insect Pinning Workshop — Insect pinning classes teach the art of prese
 rving and displaying insects\, such as butterflies and beetles\, using spe
 cialized entomology pins\, spreading boards\, and paper strips. Workshops 
 often provide specimens\, kits\, and guidance on hydrating and positioning
  wings.\n\nFeatured musical performance with AURSJOEN\, an ethereal artist
  musician based in San Francisco. https://aursjoen.bandcamp.com/album/stra
 nd\n\n Vendor participation and performers will be provided in collaborat
 ion with the Menagerie & Oddities Expo.\n\n For more information\, visit 
 https://www.visitpenngrove.com/a-midsummers-journey or call (707) 888-5659
LOCATION:Soap Caudron/Three Sisters Apothecary
URL:https://www.visitpenngrove.com/a-midsummers-journey 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
