BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Public Garden Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T140000
UID:260605nQdH1yf1jEy-tkGx9Jm55A
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a guided tour of the Occidental Arts & Ecology Cen
 ter's demonstration gardens and living landscapes. Led by rotating OAEC st
 aff\, these tours offer an opportunity to explore our diverse food\, medic
 inal\, pollinator\, and native plant gardens while learning about the ecol
 ogical principles that guide our work. \n\nWhen: Tours start at 1 pm ever
 y first and third Saturday of the month\, April through October. \n\nWher
 e: Tours start and end at the OAEC Nursery. 15290 Coleman Valley Rd\, Occi
 dental\, CA 95465. Upper Driveway. \n\nImportant Information:\n\nNo regis
 tration required—just show up!\n\nPlease use the second driveway and par
 k in the upper lot near the greenhouses.\n\nThe tour route includes steep 
 hills and unpaved dirt and gravel paths. Sturdy shoes\, a brimmed hat\, an
 d weather-appropriate layers are recommended.\n\nIf you require mobility s
 upport or have other accessibility needs\, please call ahead so we can acc
 ommodate you. Monday–Friday\, contact the main office at \\(707\\) 874-1
 557 ext. 101.\n\nA highlight of every tour is the OAEC Nursery\, a nonprof
 it nursery dedicated to uplifting ecologically and culturally important pl
 ants. The nursery features a wide selection of perennial food crops\, medi
 cinal and native plants\, and an ever-evolving collection of annual vegeta
 bles and herbs adapted to our region.
LOCATION:Occidental Arts and Ecology Center
URL:https://oaec.org/events/tours/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sturgeon’s Mill Open Demonstration Run
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T150000
UID:2606059KROeeTspkenlGbQaeGSBg
DESCRIPTION:Step into a true piece of California history at Sturgeon’s M
 ill\, a fully operational **steam-powered sawmill founded in 1914**. Unlik
 e a replica\, this is an authentic working museum where the **original mac
 hinery still runs today**\, offering a rare chance to see early 20th-centu
 ry industry in action.\n\n**Dates:** June 20-21 | August 1-2 | September 1
 2-13\n\n**Time:** 10:00 AM - 3:00 PM (crew breaks for lunch 12:00 PM -1:00
  PM)\n\n**Location:** 2150 Green Hill Rd\, Sebastopol\, CA\n\nWatch live s
 team demonstrations as the mill comes to life\, explore historic equipment
 \, and learn how local lumber mills helped build Sonoma County and the gre
 ater Bay Area. Docent-led tours run throughout the day\, or you can explor
 e at your own pace.\n\nCome experience the sights\, sounds\, and stories o
 f a working mill where history still runs on steam.\n\n**Highlights:**\n\n
 Live operation of a historic steam-powered sawmill\n\nAll-original equipme
 nt from over 100 years ago\n\nGuided tours and hands-on exploration\n\nBla
 cksmith shop\, gardens\, and farm animals\n\nFood available for purchase f
 rom the cook shack\n\nBring a picnic and enjoy the beautiful redwood setti
 ng\n\n**Good to Know:**\n\nAdmission is **free - no tickets required**\n\n
 Donations are appreciated to support preservation\n\nFree parking availabl
 e on site.
LOCATION:Sturgeon's Mill
URL:http://www.sturgeonsmill.com/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
