BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Secret Garden the Musical
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T170000
UID:260606d3HkiXYQ_kKBsNxDzNz4qA
DESCRIPTION:Step into a world of wonder\, mystery\, and renewal.\n\nCinnab
 ar Theater presents The Secret Garden The Musical\, the beloved story brou
 ght to life with a soaring score and breathtaking storytelling.\n\nOrphane
 d and sent to live with her reclusive uncle in a grand English manor\, you
 ng Mary Lennox discovers a hidden\, neglected garden. As she nurtures it b
 ack to life\, she awakens something magical—not only in the world around
  her\, but in the hearts of those who have long been closed off to hope.\n
 \nThis enchanting adaptation by Marsha Norman and Lucy Simon\, based on th
 e classic novel by Frances Hodgson Burnett\, is a moving tale of healing\,
  transformation\, and the power of nature.\n\n**Performance Dates & Times:
 **\n\nJune 12–June 28\, 2026\n\nFridays at 7:30 PM\n\nSaturdays at 7:30 
 PM\n\nSundays at 2:00 PM\n\nLearn more at cinnabartheater.org\n\n**Locatio
 n:**\n\nSonoma State University – Warren Theater (Ives Hall)\n\n1801 Eas
 t Cotati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA 94928\n\nRun Time:\n\nApproximately 2 hou
 rs 30 minutes\, including one 15-minute intermission\n\nRecommended For:\n
 \nAppropriate for all ages – perfect for families\n\n⸻\n\nCast:\n\nMar
 y Lennox: Violet Spears\n\nAlternate Mary Lennox: Serena Ridout\n\nColin C
 raven: Nathanael Koross\n\nAlternate Colin Craven: Joe Schulze\n\nArchibal
 d Craven: Ben Sasnett\n\nLily: Syona Ayyankeril\n\nRose / Dreamer: Katie V
 eale\n\nMartha: Nicole Stanley\n\nMrs. Medlock: Tika Moon\n\nBen Weatherst
 aff: Jonathan Spencer\n\nDickon: Beckett Hepp\n\nClaire / Dreamer: Natalie
  Burton\n\nAlice / Dreamer: Miriam Valencia\n\nMrs. Winthrop / Dreamer: Ka
 thi Brotemarkle\n\nAlbert / Dreamer: David A. Bradbury\n\nMajor Holmes & S
 helly / Dreamer: Noah Evans\n\nLt. Shaw / Dreamer: Corey Wilson\n\nLt. Wri
 ght / Dreamer: Mason Hunt\n\nNeville Craven: Zachary Hasbany\n\n⸻\n\nCre
 ative Team:\n\nJane Erwin: Director\n\nBrett Strader: Music Director\n\nBr
 idget Codoni: Choreographer\n\nElise Clark: Stage Manager\n\nJohn Sheridan
 : Assistant Stage Manager\n\nRoss Tiffany-Brown: Technical Director\n\nApr
 il George: Lighting Designer\n\nMateo Felix: Prop Designer / Co-Sound Desi
 gner\n\nDonnie Frank: Costume Designer & Hair/Makeup Designer\n\nPeter Cro
 mpton: Set Designer\n\nJohn Rustan: Dialect Coach\n\nLaurynn Malilay: Co-S
 ound Designer\n\nDiane Dragone: Executive Director\n\nNathan Cummings: Art
 istic Director\n\n⸻\n\nGetting to Sonoma State University:\n\nThe Warren
  Theater is located in Ives Hall on the Sonoma State University campus in 
 Rohnert Park. Plan to arrive early to allow time for parking and walking t
 o the venue.\n\nhttps://cinnabartheater.org/show/thesecretgarden/
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Warren Theater\, Located in Ives Hall
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/thesecretgarden/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: Callie Watts & Kris Dilbeck
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T143000
UID:260606Ypw81bM-OkiX3TolGMIuVQ
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts: Where Classic Sounds Meet Modern Soul\n\nJoin us
  for No Cell Sundays with Callie Watts\, a Northern California pop singer-
 songwriter whose sound is steeped in the golden era of songwriting.\n\nRai
 sed on classical music\, The Beatles\, and The Beach Boys\, Callie discove
 red her calling through the great writers of the '60s and '70s—Joni Mitc
 hell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy Joel\, and Carole K
 ing. These legendary artists shaped her melodic writing style and continue
  to influence every note she plays.\n\nA versatile musician\, Callie has s
 pent her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, arranger\, and lea
 d/backing vocalist—performing solo and with local and Bay Area bands acr
 oss multiple genres. Expect an afternoon of soulful melodies\, timeless cl
 assics\, and songs that transport you back to when music was everything.\n
 \nWhat's No Cell Sundays?\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your devices\, r
 econnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people around you. Check y
 our phone with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting. Bring a
  blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was meant to be
  spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-callie-watts
 -kris-dilbeck
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Solstice Soundscape Listening Walk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T213000
UID:260605_SInmVjW9EGR4G4gWk767w
DESCRIPTION:Jack Hines \\(host of the Ear to the Wild podcast on
  KRCB/NPR\\) will set up his high-tech audio equipment enabling 
 participants to listen in greater detail to the summer solstice 
 soundscape. This will be a quiet\, meditative hike\, where we wi
 ll spend most of our time listening. We will start with a shor
 t hike \\(<1 mile\\) to a quieter location where we hope to he
 ar owls and other summertime sounds such as the Common Poorwill.
  After setting up the audio equipment\, we will listen quietly 
 for ~45 minutes. Feel free to bring a portable chair \\(in a b
 ag\\). Then\, we will hike back. Owls that have been heard/seen
  previously at Sugarloaf include Great Horned Owl\, Western Scree
 ch Owl\, Barn Owl\, Northern Pygmy Owl\, Northern Saw-Whet Owl\,
  and Spotted Owl. In October 2023\, Jack recorded a Northern Py
 gmy Owl at Sugarloaf \\(https://www.eartothewild.com/heard/2023/10/29/
 krcb-segment-035-northern-pygmy-owl\\).\n\nMeet at the White Barn par
 king area. Tickets are $15 for general audiences\, $7.5 for stud
 ents\, youth \\(12-17 year olds must be accompanied by a parent
  or legal guardian\\)\, Sugarloaf  members\, Sugarloaf or RFO vo
 lunteers\, and free for children 11 and under. Tickets day-of on
  site are $20 and might not be available Wear comfortable cloth
 ing\, appropriate footwear for rocky/slippery trails\, and sun pro
 tection. Bring at least a quart of water\, and if you desire\,
  a snack\, butterfly or wildflower guides\, or a camera. Parking
  fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/summer-solstice-soundscape-listening-walk-62120
 26
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
