BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Caldwell Snyder Gallery Exhibition Featuring Gilles Marrey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T170000
UID:260518VM_KbwBWhky2-gCQ5lafpw
DESCRIPTION:Caldwell Snyder Gallery is pleased to present Between Day & N
 ight\, an exhibition of new works by acclaimed Parisian painter Gilles Mar
 rey\, on display from May 30th – June 21st at the gallery’s historic S
 tar Building location in St. Helena. Known for his atmospheric depictions 
 of contemporary life\, Marrey transforms familiar interiors\, urban street
 scapes\, and landscapes into emotionally resonant scenes through luminous 
 palettes of violets\, blues\, pinks\, and warm oranges. His paintings invi
 te viewers to slow down and reconsider everyday environments with renewed 
 attention and sensitivity.\n\nInfluenced by years of travel throughout the
  Bay Area and inspired in part by the work of Richard Diebenkorn\, Marrey
 ’s practice explores the relationship between structure\, light\, atmosp
 here\, and lived experience. Trained in France during the 1980s\, he devel
 oped a distinctive figurative style rooted in observation while remaining 
 deeply contemporary in feeling and execution. Set within the heart of Napa
  Valley\, the exhibition offers visitors an opportunity to experience Marr
 ey’s richly layered works in an intimate gallery setting while celebrati
 ng the intersection of contemporary art\, place\, and atmosphere.\n\n1328 
 Main St\, St Helena\, CA 94574\n\n707.200.5050\n\nMonday – Saturday 10am
  – 5pm\n\nSunday 11am – 5pm
LOCATION:Caldwell Snyder Gallery
URL:https://www.caldwellsnyder.com/artists/gilles-marrey
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
