BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T170000
UID:2605297D3ze5lGkE2iBj6zTa1g2g
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lavender Labyrinth Sound Bath Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T200000
UID:260526ELuDUwYcJk69uY-Wb18tZg
DESCRIPTION:Join us in our most dreamy location yet\, in the center of a l
 avender labyrinth for an exquisite sunset sound Bath Experience!\n\nJoin u
 s in our most dreamy location yet\, in the middle of lavender labyrinth at
  sunset!\n\nMondays through October 6th\n\nWe are thrilled to share this m
 agic with you! Let the fragrance of lavender fill and sooth your senses as
  the sound expands your awareness.\n\nSound baths create the space for sel
 f-healing and transformation. The resonance of the instruments is not just
  an auditory experience ~ it's like receiving a full body sound massage.\n
 \nThere will be 8 Gongs\, Crystal singing bowls\, Hand pan\, Mono chord\, 
 Chimes galore\, Ocean drum\, Native drum\, Angelic Vocals & more.The vibra
 tions will transport you on a powerful healing journey!\n\nPLEASE NOTE: Th
 e sound bath starts at 7pm. Gates close at 6:45 PM. Please be Mindful of t
 iming. You will need time to park\, walk up and set up. You are welcome to
  come walk the labyrinth and visit the Farm Stand from 6 pm onward. Please
  check the hourly weather so you are prepaired. You will be lying on the g
 rass\, so please bring all that you will need to feel cozy and warm\, "yog
 a mat" or camping pad\, "Blanket" or sleeping bag\, a pillow\, eye mask\, 
 and water bottle. Wonderful Lavender Eye Masks will be available to purcha
 se for $25 by the Bees & Blooms Farm Stand.\n\nIf we have environmental Ci
 rcumstance such as rain or unhealthy air quality due to fires we will post
 pone to Wednesday of the same week and your tickets will roll over to that
  day. If these conditions are present it is your responsibility to monitor
  your emails(also junk/spam) for notifications. In these force of nature s
 ituations Tickets are not refundable but are transferable! Your understand
 ing and cooperation is greatly appreciated.\n\nPlease be informed that the
 re are bee hives on site and there may be bees on the lavender plants. If 
 you are allergic to bee stings\, bring your Epipen. An incident is unlikel
 y\, but best to be prepared. Also\, at some point\, probably mid July the 
 Lavender will began to be harvested so there may be less lavender towards 
 the end of the month.Full Bloom occurs mid June. The last sound bath of th
 e Lavender season will be Oct. 6th. The labyrinth & farm will be beautiful
  however the Lavender will be reaching the end of its cycle around mid. Ju
 ly. You will walk through many rows of a varity of blooming flowers on you
  way from parking.\n\nOnly disability trained Registered Service dogs are 
 permitted because of the animals on the farm and the nature of the Sound B
 ath. Your understanding is appreciated. Also\, please no children under 10
  years of age.\n\nLabyrinths represent a metaphor for your life path and t
 he journey you are making. While walking the path of the labyrinth\, eithe
 r alone or with a group\, focus on your feelings and emotions to allow you
  to connect with yourself. You may also want to choose a meditation that y
 ou are comfortable with in order to clear and quiet your mind. The uses of
  a labyrinth are many\; relief from stress and anxiety\, healing\, meditat
 ion\, problem solving\, enhancing intuition\, expanding thought processes\
 , communicating with the Divine\, balancing mind\, body and spirit\, letti
 ng go of unwanted energies\, obtaining goals\, celebrating and remembering
  others\, building trust in yourself or others\, and coping with grief\, s
 orrow and loss. The labyrinth is an ancient symbol that relates to wholene
 ss. It combines the imagery of the circle and the spiral into a meandering
  but purposeful path. The Labyrinth represents a journey to our own center
  and back again out into the world. Labyrinths have long been used as medi
 tation and prayer tools.\n\nLooking forward to sharing this Extraordinary 
 Experience with you! In Gratitude
LOCATION:Bees n blooms 
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1985876807991?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
