BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Art of Letting Go: Intuitive Ink Painting & the Zen Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T160000
UID:2606073XwnRfTZYkiD39jhY3MbnQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nStep into a calming\, immersive workshop where intuition
  guides the brush and imperfection becomes a source of beauty. Blending Ea
 stern and Western approaches to abstraction\, this experience weaves toget
 her meditation\, movement\, and expressive mark-making to create deeply pe
 rsonal paintings. Rooted in the Japanese aesthetic of wabi-sabi\, particip
 ants release the need for perfection and explore the unexpected through in
 k\, watercolor\, and gesture. The session begins with gentle centering\, t
 hen moves into practices like painting the ensō&mdash\;the Zen circle sym
 bolizing presence and wholeness&mdash\;using Asian brushes and layered tec
 hniques to build atmosphere\, depth\, and emotion. No prior experience is 
 needed&mdash\;just a willingness to slow down\, connect\, and create from 
 within.\n\nThis workshop is located in the classroom.\n\nAbout the Teacher
 : \n\nSherrie Lovler holds a B.A. in Studio Art and has taught calligraphy
  and related arts for decades at institutions including Ghost Ranch\, La R
 omita School of Art in Italy\, Northern Arizona University\, and major cal
 ligraphy guilds and conferences. She is the author\, illustrator\, and des
 igner of On Softer Ground\, an IPPY gold medal winner for book design\, an
 d her latest book\,Distant Voices\, explores art as a collaboration with n
 ature\, memory\, and unseen influences. She is an Art at the Source and Ar
 t Trails artist and recently had a solo exhibit at Gallery Route One in Po
 int Reyes Station.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-intuitive-ink-
 painting?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
