BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exploring Color
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T160000
UID:260607LbmuU-xNTkWw9aPqCfZQFw
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nIn this 3-hour workshop\, participants will explore the 
 fundamentals of color theory using acrylic paint\, starting with the prima
 ry colors and expanding into a rich spectrum of hues through guided color 
 mixing. Students will experiment with blending\, gradation\, and observing
  how colors interact\, discovering a wide range of tones and subtle variat
 ions between them. Through playful exploration and simple exercises\, the 
 workshop encourages curiosity\, confidence\, and a deeper understanding of
  how color can be used for expression. No prior painting experience is nec
 essary&mdash\;this accessible\, hands-on workshop welcomes participants of
  all levels to engage with color in a meaningful and creative way.\n\nThis
  workshop is located in the classroom.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nEsther Hi
 lsenrad is a Bay Area&ndash\;based artist and educator originally from New
  York City\, with over 23 years of teaching experience across a wide range
  of subjects and age groups. Her career has spanned formal classroom teach
 ing\, museum education\, and work as a teaching artist. Now working indepe
 ndently\, Esther teaches art camps from her home studio\, afterschool art 
 classes\, and private lessons for elementary-aged children. Her deepest pa
 ssion lies in art education&mdash\;guiding others to feel confident expres
 sing themselves creatively and exploring diverse artistic mediums. In her 
 own artistic practice\, Esther enjoys experimenting with color theory thro
 ugh acrylic painting\, crafting miniature scenes from recycled materials\,
  and creating jewelry and other crafts. Her work is driven by a genuine lo
 ve of both making art and helping others discover their creative voice.\n\
 nTo learn more about Esther:\n\nwww.esthertheartteacher.com\n\nww.estherhe
 artsart.com\n\n@esthertheartteacher\n\n@estherheartsart
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-exploring-color
 ?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Idea to Object: Inside the Product Design Process
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T200000
UID:260607JnFXCWONe0aFH3blLn4GnQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13 and over\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nThis engaging presentation ex
 plores how product designers transform ideas into tangible objects through
  a thoughtful process of development and prototyping. From early concept s
 ketches to iterative testing and refinement\, you'll gain insight into the
  tools\, methods\, and mindset behind successful design. Featuring real-wo
 rld examples\, the talk highlights how creativity\, problem-solving\, and 
 user experience come together to shape the products we use every day. Idea
 l for anyone curious about the journey from concept to creation.\n\nThis l
 ecture is located in the Main Gallery.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nMarty Mar
 fin is a Sonoma County&ndash\;based maker\, educator\, and fabricator with
  extensive experience across education\, media\, and museum production. He
  currently serves as Innovative Arts Makerspace Manager at the Academy of 
 Innovative Arts in Forestville and as Community Engagement Representative 
 and grant writer at Chimera Arts. His past roles include Maker Media Lab M
 anager at Maker Media and Model Making Studio Manager at the California Co
 llege of the Arts\, where he supported thousands of student projects. With
  a background spanning sculpture\, prototyping\, and exhibit design\, Mart
 y has created immersive museum installations for institutions including th
 e American Museum of Natural History and the Field Museum.\n\nLearn more a
 bout Marty:\n\nwww.martymarfin.com
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-product-design-
 survey?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Art Playground
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T160000
UID:260604ZPzPZH3g-EKovBfgz-SqqA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nDive into the world of digital art without the steep lea
 rning curve! This course is a creative playground designed for curious min
 ds of all ages. We're ditching the complex technical jargon and focusing p
 urely on experimentation\, play\, and discovery. You'll get hands-on exper
 ience with a diverse suite of accessible\, easy-to-use software to bring y
 our imagination to life. Go from sketching your first digital illustration
 s to sculpting beginner-friendly 3D models and bringing characters to life
  with simple animation. Bring your curiosity\, jump in\, and let's make so
 me art!\n\nThis class is located in the Main Gallery. \n\nStudents bring:\
 n\nLaptops\n\nPAC provides: \n\nExtension Chords\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\
 nLije Morgan teaches animation\, 3D\, and game design\, and offers private
  lessons for artists exploring new media. Their work examines the power of
  &ldquo\;cute&rdquo\; aesthetics as tools of persuasion and subversion\, o
 ften blending 2D and 3D techniques using Blender. Passionate about storyte
 lling through games and animation\, Lije also creates live visuals for per
 formances and hosts Boiled Over\, a podcast featuring independent animator
 s from around the world.\n\nLearn more: \n\nwww.lije.com@lije.mo
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-digital-art-pl
 ayground?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
