BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine and Wheel
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T210000
UID:2606020F3z8QeLeUC94HGjCcjXAw
DESCRIPTION:Date & Time\n\nEvent Series \\(See All\\)\n\nFriday\, June 5\,
  2026 from 6:00 pm to 9:00 pm\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\
 nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categories: Ceramics\, Workshops\
 n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n21 and older\n\nRegistration\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$65
 \n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$65\n\nA per
 fect gift for you and a loved one. Try your hand at the potter’s wheel a
 nd enjoy some local wine and cheese while you’re at it!\n\nAbout the Cla
 ss\n\nEver wanted to try your hand at the potter’s wheel\, but not quite
  ready to dive into an 8 week class yet? Our Wine and Wheel nights offer t
 he best environment to dabble in this new endeavor\, while enjoying some l
 ocal wine and cheese while you’re at it. Sign up yourself and a partner\
 , friend\, sibling… to experience it together! Wine and Wheel students a
 re able to keep one creation of their choosing from the evening to have it
  fired and glazed by the Sonoma Ceramics staff and made ready for pickup. 
 A perfect gift for you and a loved one! Please note: each ticket is only f
 or 1 adult\, if you are signing up 2 people\, please choose quantity 2 at 
 checkout.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/wine-and-wheel-2/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broadway Under the Stars - Ain't Too Proud: The Life and Times of 
 the Temptations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T220000
UID:2605288HV54Pz0TkSQR9ibtENGZA
DESCRIPTION:Ain’t Too Proud is the Tony-winning\, electrifying musical t
 hat follows The Temptations’ extraordinary journey from the streets of D
 etroit to the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame. Featuring their signature dance mo
 ves and unforgettable harmonies\, this musical takes audiences behind the 
 music: how the group formed\, the unprecedented chart-topping success they
  achieved \\(42 Top Ten hits\, 14 \\#1 singles\\)\, and the personal and p
 olitical tensions that threatened their unity during a turbulent era in Am
 erica. This thrilling story of brotherhood\, family loyalty and betrayal i
 s set to the beat of the group’s treasured hits\, including “My Girl\,
 ” “Just My Imagination\,” “Get Ready\,” “Papa Was a Rolling St
 one” and so many more\, with a book by award-winning playwright Dominiqu
 e Morisseau \\(Skeleton Crew\, Paradise Blue\\) adapted from Williams’s 
 1988 memoir. The New York Times praised the show as\, “Pretty close to p
 erfect”\, with The Washington Post proclaiming it was “Dazzling and El
 ectrifying.” Ain’t Too Proud is presented through special arrangement 
 with Music Theatre International \\(MTI\\). All authorized performance mat
 erials are also supplied by MTI. www.mtishows.com Music Theatre Internatio
 nal gives Ain’t Too Proud: The Life and Times of the Temptations a PG13 
 rating. This production is a gritty\, authentic look at the history of The
  Temptations. Parental discretion is advised.
LOCATION:Field Of Dreams
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/27668377922754317/27668377962754313/?a
 ctive_tab=about
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
